Speridlabs IDOL integration notice

Image preprocessing, image conditioning, camera decoding, and sampling
equations in this family are modified from:

  speridlabs/idol-sdk
  https://github.com/speridlabs/idol-sdk
  revision 4702a7f00850e34b6e83a2170cc123c3e9570744

Those portions are provided under the accompanying Apache License 2.0
(LICENSE-APACHE-2.0). Ported source files carry a prominent modification notice.

IDOL's networks keep the architecture of VAST-AI-Research TripoSplat (MIT),
which upstream credits. They run as this package's TripoSplat classes; see
../triposplat/NOTICE. Upstream's denoiser source also credits the Diffusers
Wan transformer (Apache-2.0). No IDOL network code is copied here.

The DINOv3 image encoder runs as the stock Transformers DINOv3ViTModel and the
Flux.2 VAE encoder on stock Diffusers blocks.

Not included:

- the BiRefNet background remover (upstream bundles BiRefNet weights,
  birefnet.safetensors, from ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet, MIT);
- training code, the Gradio demo, and upstream's PLY writer.

Weights are not redistributed. The speridlabs/idol model card declares
Apache-2.0 and the repository is not gated. IDOL also needs two image encoders
that it does not bundle:

- facebook/dinov3-vith16plus-pretrain-lvd1689m, gated, under the DINOv3
  License;
- the FLUX.2 VAE from black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-dev, which is gated under the
  FLUX non-commercial license.

A converted folder embeds both encoders. Check their terms before
redistributing it.

No affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement by Speridlabs, VAST-AI-Research,
Meta, or Black Forest Labs is claimed.
